.TH SWAYDESK-SWITCHER 1 2026-11-14 "swaydesk 0.1.2" "Sway desktop components"
.SH NAME
swaydesk\-switcher \- Alt+Tab window switcher for Sway
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B swaydesk\-switcher
daemon
.br
.B swaydesk\-switcher
next
.br
.B swaydesk\-switcher
prev
.SH DESCRIPTION
Switches windows in the order of use, with a card in the middle of the screen showing the icon, title and workspace of each window. Releasing Alt focuses the chosen window; Esc cancels. A quick tap does not show the card.
.PP
The session runs it under the name sway\-switcher (a link in the package's helper directory to /usr/bin/swaydesk\-switcher); the process name is sway\-switcher too.
.SH NOTES
.TP
.B next, prev
They signal the resident process (SIGUSR1 and SIGUSR2) and exit. Without it, they walk the Sway tree without the card.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B daemon
The resident process, started by the Sway configuration: it keeps the order of use.
.TP
.B next
Alt+Tab: the window used before; again, the next one.
.TP
.B prev
Alt+Shift+Tab: the oldest window; again, the previous one.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Exit 0 at once without doing anything: the Python launchers use it to check that the binary and its libraries load.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/sway\-desktop/config.toml
The desktop configuration: language, accent color, GTK and icon themes, folder color, file manager, weather location and holidays.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sway (5),
.BR swaydesk (7)
